course: dictionary
lesson: 9427
title: Stabiliser: the word that keeps things steady
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stabiliser is something that keeps another thing steady, so it does not tip over or wobble. Context gives you the clue: «Stabilisers stop the bike tipping, so children never practise steering into a lean.» The words bike and tipping tell you that a stabiliser stops something falling over.
explain: Look at the word stop in that sentence. A stabiliser holds something back from moving badly. It does not push the bike forward. Ask yourself what the thing does, then try your meaning in the sentence: "Stabilisers keep the bike steady" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: One word can mean different things in different places. On a bike, a stabiliser is a small wheel. On a ship, it is a fin. On a food label, it is an ingredient. The words around it show you which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A stabiliser is any part or device that keeps something steady.
fact: «Stabilisers» are the two small extra wheels on the back of a child's bicycle that stop it falling over (US: training wheels).
fact: The fins on a ship and the small horizontal wings at the back of an aeroplane are also stabilisers, because they keep the vehicle balanced.
fact: On food labels, a stabiliser is added to keep a mixture blended and stop it changing, for example in ice cream.
fact: Phrases you may hear are "take off the stabilisers" and "ride without stabilisers".
exercise: «Stabilisers stop the bike tipping, so children never practise steering into a lean.» What do stabilisers do on a bike? | They are the pedals | They paint the bike | *They stop the bike falling over | They make the bike go faster
exercise: The fins on a ship and the small wings at the back of an aeroplane both do what job? | *Keep the vehicle steady | Hold the food | Carry the passengers | Make the vehicle change colour
exercise: Sam reads on a label: «Stabilisers are listed among the ingredients in ice cream.» What is a stabiliser in ice cream? | *A substance that keeps the mixture blended and stops it changing | A type of spoon | A small wheel for the cone | A flavour that makes it sweet
test: «Ride without stabilisers» is a phrase that means: | Ride a bike very fast | *Ride a bike without the small extra back wheels | Ride a horse without a saddle | Ride without a helmet
test: «Balance bikes with no pedals teach children faster.» Which is the best reason? | They have stabilisers to help children | *They have no pedals, so children learn balance and steering first | They have bigger wheels for going faster | They are only for adults
exam: A stabiliser is best described as: | A kind of paint for ships | A type of food only | Pedals that make a bike move | *A part or device that keeps something steady
